A||||9||JohnnyK||Push button radio parts. Where?||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||12-04-2000||11:19 PM||||I need to find the little rubber pieces that go behind the buttons (volume, station, balance) on the all push button radio (the little rubber pieces that push against the actual chip, and maybe the plastic that the rubber things sit in). Think I could get these from an electronic store? i kind of doubt it. Anyone have a junker radio but with working buttons? Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||JohnnyK||12-05-2000||01:46 PM||||Throwing it back up. Someone has got to know.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||12-05-2000||03:27 PM||||Johnny,<P>I don't think you'll have any luck trying to find just the little "rubber" parts (They are actually carbon impregnated contactors). I went through this on my first Fiero. I had to buy the entire module replaced and the only way they would sell it to me is if I paid THEM to install it. That was back in 1989ish and it cost about $90 then.<P>The company is called Tecni-car Inc. The last number I have for them is 1-800-822-0022. This is the company that repairs all the Delco radios for the local dealerships. You may try asking your local GM dealership who they send their radios to when warrenty repair is needed.<P>Good Luck,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnnyK||12-05-2000||03:40 PM||||Don't think an electronic store would have them eh? Would just normal pieces of rubber work, or do they serve a specific job (conducting)?||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfixit58||12-05-2000||05:12 PM||||No. Regular rubber will not work.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Feenx||12-05-2000||06:38 PM||||You might want to check the wreckers<BR>I've seen 3 Fieros (not sure what years) in Kichener at discount Auto Wreckers.<BR>they may have the same radio you have...||||reg||1
Z||000006||lawrence||12-05-2000||09:38 PM||||Those rubber buttons have a layer of carbon conductor on them that eventually rubs off.  You might be able to find some teeny tiny switches to put behind those rubber pieces, like I did with a cordless phone and my TV remote control (look in the mag).<P>If you can't find any switches, you might be able to glue some flattened aluminum foil onto the rubber pads.  This won't last as long because the cement usually gives out, but at least you'll have something.<P>Good luck,<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://www.webelectricmagazine.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.webelectricmagazine.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||JohnnyK||12-05-2000||10:38 PM||||Well, the rubber sort of broke. I guess you could say it's a "top hat" shape, and the top of the hat broke off on some of them.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||12-05-2000||11:07 PM||||JohnnyK,<BR>I've got a manual for that radio. It's buried in a box, somewhere. I think I've seen it *once* since I moved. I promised some info to someone else, too. I'll renew my search for it. Maybe I can get you a part #. Do you already have the panel taken apart?<BR>There's a place in north Atlanta that used to sell the whole assembly, -circuit board, rubber "buttons", the plastic pushbuttons, and the front panel that covered 'em all. The buttons were black instead of gray, tho'. Seems like the whole thing was like $90.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>I'll see if I can dig up all that info.<P>Raydar||||reg||1
Z||000009||rockcrawl||12-07-2000||06:37 PM||||I talked toa guy at a local radio shop here, and the guy basically said the GM Push-button radios were junk from the start. The only good thing about them is the upside-down mounted Blaupunkt-made cassette unit. Anyway, he said the button assy is non-repairable. He was not interested in selling parts without service, but he did say the new pushbutton assy was $38. The pushbutton radios were not only used in Fieros. This guy had three of them on his shelf.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
